  "summary": "The h2 crate, used internally by hyper, had a flaw that would accept and queue empty DATA frames without limit.",
  "details": "The h2 crate, used internally by hyper, had a flaw that would accept and queue empty DATA frames without limit.\nIf streams were not actively drained, this could lead to unbounded memory usage, or a panic if the length overflows.\n\nLow severity.\n\nPatched in v0.4.16.",
